#~
Fuzzer finding against v2026.9.4 (x64 Windows), hand-minimized from the
reduce.py output s3_nil_deref_funcref_seed231.obs in this directory.

signature (of the fuzzer's program): diverge: s0/off,s0/jit1 | s3/off,s3/default,s3/jit1
  first=F#=# vs  exit 1 >>> Attempting to dereference a 'Nil' memory element <<< @FuzzProgram->F0(a:Int)

Compiled at s3, this program never finishes under any VM configuration
(--jit=off, the default, --jit=1: all time out), so it is the optimizer's
output that is wrong, not a JIT. Compiled at s0 it prints F0=864749906 at
once. With the dead Int locals of the seed-231 program the same method ends in
"Attempting to dereference a 'Nil' memory element" instead.

The ingredients, found by deleting one at a time: a counted `for` loop over an
array and a local holding a static function reference `(Int) ~ Int`, in the
same method. Without the loop, or without the function-reference local, s3 is
correct.

Expected output: F0=864749906
~#

